Revision history for Game-Go

0.02    2026-10-10
        - The board is drawn as a board: grid lines and star points, with
          stones on the intersections.
        - Point at the move you mean: the arrow keys walk a cursor over the
          board and the line under it says what the move would take, what
          liberties it would have, or why it cannot be played.
        - Fix: the last move was marked by wrapping an already-coloured cell,
          so the mark was emitted on every board and never once visible. It
          is a ringed stone now, and a point a capture emptied is an x.
        - Fix: an answer, a refusal or a redrawn board landed on the prompt's
          own line off a terminal.

0.01    2026-09-18
        First version
